PORTIONS DERIVED FROM PEARCLEANER
---------------------------------

The following components are substantially based on Pearcleaner's source:

  * App-residual scanning algorithms
    - AppPathFinder class (forward scan: find paths related to a given app)
    - ReversePathFinder class (reverse scan: find residuals not claimed by
      any installed app)
    - Sensitivity tier model (.strict / .enhanced / .deep)

  * Curated data tables
    - `skipReverse` — daemon/system names excluded from orphan scan
    - `conditions`, `skipConditions` — per-app include/exclude rules
    - `skipDeepSearch` — bundle IDs that opt out of deep matching
    - `reverseLocations` — Library directories enumerated for orphan scan
    - `standardLibrarySubdirectories` — recognized Library subdirs

  * Code-signing extraction
    - SecCode / SecStaticCode entitlement and team-identifier reading
      (loadAppInfo / getEntitlements / getTeamIdentifier)

  * String/path normalization
    - `String.normalized()` (alphanumeric-lowercase canonicalization for
      substring matching)

MODIFICATIONS IN cleaner
------------------------

The following work was done independently for this project:

  * Ported from a SwiftUI macOS application to a single-file Swift CLI
    (`#!/usr/bin/env swift cleaner.swift`).
  * Added a unified interactive checkbox selector (alternate screen buffer,
    arrow keys, wasd/hjkl alias, inverse-video cursor row).
  * Added new modules not present in Pearcleaner:
      - pkg     — uninstall macOS .pkg packages via lsbom/pkgutil receipts
      - plugin  — list/uninstall plugins (QuickLook, Spotlight, Audio Unit, etc.)
      - devenv  — scan/uninstall dev-tool caches (npm, Cargo, Xcode, etc.)
  * Restructured into 8 PART sections with explicit shared-vs-local
    boundaries (see file header).
  * Section-headed default-selection model for app-uninstall (STRICT default
    on, ENHANCED / DEEP default off).
